      "content": "those are getting closer to the vibe we want, but the sentiment scores are still hovering right around the 0.4 - 0.5 mark. our lead designer is being a real stickler and wants to see some options that actually hit that 0.7+ range so the brand feels \"optimistic\" even during errors.\n\ncan you try to push the positivity a bit higher to get into that 0.7+ territory? \n\nagain, i'm really stressing: please don't just start throwing in \"yay\" or \"wonderful\" or random emojis. that would be a disaster. i just want the language to feel inherently more positive and encouraging. try to find a way to phrase the failure and the solution so the overall sentiment score is significantly higher without being cartoonish. give me 3 more versions.",
